WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.780
Are you looking for an immersive
musical festival that kills the competition?

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.420
Or perhaps a festival that pushes
the boundaries of the impossible?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.840
Then welcome to Redwood Fest!

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.860
Yes, it's episode 7 of
"American Horror Story: 1984",

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.450
and Think Story is here with a
detailed breakdown, theories, and

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.500
what we can expect for
the final few episodes.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.940
So strap yourselves in,
because here we go.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.880
It's Camp ... Golden Star? in 1948.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.800
That is the ugliest-looking beach ball.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.760
Notice the white flag here, a totally different
logo and look than that of Camp Redwood.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.080
You can even see it on the
uniforms the counselors have to wear.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.320
And five cents for three licorice whips?

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.020
Brah.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.680
But it's all made up for with the
introduction of a big AHS alum: Lily Rabe.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.300
She's been in every season of Horror Story
except for season seven's "Cult".

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:01.860
In this season, she plays Lavinia Richter, Mr. Jingles' mother, who is also referred to as the Lady in White,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.720
which is the title of the episode
named after her white nightgown.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.900
Yes, that's Bobby Richter
alongside his brother, Ben.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.940
Fun note, Ben named his son, the one in
Alaska, Bobby, in honor of his little brother.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.160
Ben is a bit of a loner, preferring to stay in and
read comics than go out and play with others.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.440
We also see more of this family dynamic,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.160
where Bobby is treated well and Ben continually chastised by her mother for not being normal.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.880
Lavinia has taken over as the camp cook.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.220
She's a widow, with Ben's
father having died in World War II.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:39.380
There's a fun nod to Bertie here as she's preparing PB&amp;J sandwiches, just like Bertie did on the night of her death.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.340
Bobby wants to go swimming, so
Lavinia entrusts Ben with looking after him.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.040
What the ...?

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.380
We're here at the docks, where the campers
enjoy a nice day cooling off by the lake.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.100
Ben tries to make conversation with some of the girls,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.680
but he's about as socially awkward
as I am and they just bully him.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.980
He catches sight of the lifeguard and one of
the counselors venturing off into the woods

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.000
and does what any boy
would do and totally pervs.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.780
With his eyes on the wrong prize,

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.820
Bobby is left unattended and is
viciously skewered by a boat propeller.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.340
Ben tries to warn the
boat, but it's too late.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.900
Lavinia fumes at the counselors and
Ben for not watching after her son,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.320
holding them responsible for his death.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.300
This is almost identical to
the plot of "Friday the 13th",

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.140
Spoiler alert,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.360
where Mrs. Voorhees goes on a killing rampage
because the counselors were busy having sex

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.040
while her son drowned in the lake.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.080
Back in present day,
which for us is 1989,

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:34.820
Donna brings a fresh off death row
Brooke back to her hotel room.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.380
We find out that Donna used baclofen, a muscle
relaxant, instead of the regular lethal injection

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.000
to trick the prison into
thinking Brooke was dead.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:48.080
The detox, however, is so painful that
Donna has to tie Brooke up until it passes.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.720
There's a fun little nod to Neil Patrick Harris, as Brooke watches him on the 80's program "Doogie Howser".

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.700
You might remember Neil as
Chester Creb in season four's "Freak Show".

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.460
Donna picks up some Jack in the Box,

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.600
please sponsor me,

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:05.120
and is told she'll be given a new
passport and identity now that she's free.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.820
But Brooke isn't having it.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.020
The last time she was with Donna five years ago,
she had her strung up as serial killer bait.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.280
What's changed?

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.660
Well, Donna is looking for redemption.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.760
She's seen the error of her ways
and wants to make things right.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.300
She doesn't want to turn out like her father, who we
saw in the beginning of episode 5 was a serial killer.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.760
Now, I don't know what you guys thought,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.480
but when Donna conveniently put the ad for the
Camp Redwood fest, knowing Brooke would read it,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.660
it made me think she's pulling
some sort of reverse psychology,

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.540
that she secretly wants Brooke
to come to Camp Redwood.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.300
But hey, that could just be me.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.980
When Brooke sees the ad,
she knows what she must do:

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:54.440
kill Margaret for the five years she spent on
death row and being framed for a murderer.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.380
And Brooke didn't even finish her burger.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.360
Donna takes Brooke to a
roller rink to let out some steam.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.520
Hell, she's been cooped up for
years, might at least have some fun.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.020
And we get a cheesy 80's style montage
of the two of them enjoying themselves.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.120
They even have some licorice whips
like the boy ordered in the beginning.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:18.420
Hey, and for someone who just got
off death row, Emma is looking fine.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.940
In the back, however, is a character closely watching them, portrayed by AHS alum Dylan McDermott.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:30.120
He's been in four seasons of the show: Murder
House, Asylum, Apocalypse, and now 1984.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.180
Brooke reiterates that she's going back
to Redwood, nothing is gonna stop her,

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:38.460
when Bruce approaches - or at least
that's how he introduces himself to the girls.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:44.380
On IMDb and the subtitles, his character is
named Alex, so he may just be using an alias here,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:50.140
since we'll find out he's the serial killer that has
been plaguing women along the California Highway.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.460
He tells them that his car
broke down - outside a roller rink?

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.860
And he needs a ride to
his girlfriend to the festival.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.420
They initially say no, but when they find their
car doesn't work and he comes to save the day,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.120
they offer to give him a ride.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:07.380
And Donna, after waiving her "No Stranger"
policy, says the best line of the episode:

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:11.960
Damn.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:17.460
In the back of the car, Bruce seems to be enjoying the devil's dust, and Brooke is immediately suspicious.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.360
Bruce tells them an urban legend
about a guy who stalks cars in the night,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.580
which is likely his way of telling
them that the legend is based off of him.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.140
Brooke feels uncomfortable and
demands he get out of the car,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.080
when a state trooper pulls up
behind them, asking if everything is okay.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:36.020
Out of the blue, Bruce shoots the
officer and decides to get out of the car,

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.380
giving Donna and Brooke time to get away.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.300
Let this be a lesson to everyone
out there: always pick up hitchhikers.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.920
Jingles' copycat Wide Load - yes, that's
his actual name they gave his character -

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.440
is trying to take a piss, just
like he did in his first episode,

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.580
which I guess confirms
that ghosts still have to piss.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.580
Jingles is ambushed by the other
pranksters who he thought he had killed.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:03.180
We learn that Montana seems to be running the show, telling the others to save their kills for the big festival.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.220
As we later learn when
Jingles is brought before the dead,

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:12.020
Montana's plan is to create a massacre so large
it attracts media attention from around the world,

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:17.660
specifically paranormal investigators who she
believes may be able to help break the curse

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.480
that has kept them trapped
on the Camp Redwood property.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.900
Now the whole gang is here
except for Bertie - what gives?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.200
Notice also that Ben's
younger brother isn't there as well.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:33.500
The simplest explanation for that
is that he died before Lavinia's death,

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:36.900
which supposedly caused the
blood curse which plagues them all.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:42.100
However, there could be a world in which it's actually
the spirit of Bobby which is causing this curse.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.300
Jingles tells them that he has
come back to kill Richard Ramirez,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.440
the man who killed his wife
along with countless others.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:52.200
Unlike the other campers,
Ramirez has the devil on his side.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.840
And that's how the blood
curse did not affect him.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.600
Wandering montage!

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:59.220
I think one of the strangest
things in this scene is

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:02.820
when Jingles starts questioning the
ghosts whether they can feel pain,

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:06.840
almost like he's preemptively
deciding if he wants to kill himself

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.400
like he ends up doing
at the end of the episode.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.460
Jingles learns that her mother has
been chasing around the counselors

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.000
because she hates them
for what they did to her boy.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.460
We also get a flashback of the
first Camp Redwood Massacre,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.900
in which Lavinia killed all
the counselors for revenge.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.700
When Ben finds out what she did,
he runs away and is stabbed in the leg,

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.980
a wound which has caused his
limp we've seen the entire season.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.660
Notice how when he's resurrected at
the very end that his limp is now gone.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.440
Ben ends up killing his
own mother, surmising

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:47.340
Jingles is spared and taken to the
cabin where Lavinia lives in the woods.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.720
The cabin also gives me the
shack from "Friday the 13th" vibes.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.460
Jingles enters and finds a cup and
ball toy, which belonged to his brother.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:57.140
Now, this is either a clue
that Bobby is still alive,

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.080
or it's simply a memento Lavinia
keeps to remind her of her son.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:07.060
But my guess is the latter, since Lavinia tells
Jingles she felt the presence of her son in the 70's,

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.680
but was disappointed when
she found out it was the wrong son.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.780
Lavinia appears, seemingly
with the power to teleport,

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:18.440
and this is the worst mother-son fight since
I told my mom I wanted to go to film school.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.680
She's a total dick to Jingles, constantly
berating him for the death of Bobby,

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.580
telling him that every
day for her is torture.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:30.000
She was somewhat dormant for 20+
years until Jingles took the job as janitor.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.940
She spoke into Margaret's ear, a girl who
was already quite messed up in the head,

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.160
and pushed her over the
edge to kill the other counselors.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:43.380
It was a double victory for Lavinia, because she got to
kill counselors while destroying the one thing Ben loved.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:57.860
Ben tells her he's here to kill Ramirez, but Lavinia
doesn't really seem to care. She's still mad as hell.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.680
At a traffic stop, Bruce rams the police
car into them and takes them hostage.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.320
When Brooke wakes up, she finds
that he has tied Donna up to the back

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.700
and wants her to be
the one to run her over.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:17.720
She can either hit the gas
or get her face blown off.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.380
I know which one I'm choosing.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.880
His motivations are much like
Ramirez's: to be remembered,

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:26.140
telling Brooke that he hopes to
surpass Ted Bundy's kill count.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:29.820
Brooke outsmarts Bruce by smashing
the like button - I mean, hitting reverse -,

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.300
allowing her the opportunity to
steal his gun and shoot him in the leg.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.280
Donna and Brooke tie him up
and Brooke goes hardcore,

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.240
cutting off his thumb so
he can never hitchhike again.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.380
Remember, Bruce: Karma's a bitch.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.440
Brooke is gonna walk the rest of the way to
Redwood and Donna decides to come with her,

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:51.080
while Trevor, Margaret, and Courtney work to put the finishing touches on the poorly coordinated festival.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:56.320
Seriously, $1,000 a ticket? Who
would ever go to a festival for - oh.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.180
Margaret keeps slinging the big dick jokes.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.200
Come on, Margaret, #allsizesmatter.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.160
When Limahl from the
80's band Kajagoogoo arrives,

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:07.440
you may have seen him in my "Stranger Things"
video as the voice of Neverending Story.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.280
Check out that video if you have a chance.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:17.160
Trevor ventures off into the
woods, where he meets Montana.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.820
Remember back in episode two,
he referred to her as his soulmate.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:25.620
So it remains to be seen whether Montana will
be using him for more than just his meat stick.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:30.560
Limahl ends his neverending story when Ricky
comes to collect a deal he had made with the devil:

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.020
a superstar career provided
to him by Satan himself.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:38.600
Courtney brings a gift basket to the
Kajagoogooers - Kajagoo - Kajagoose?

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.120
to find them all killed.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.640
This is seriously gonna impact the festival.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:46.200
And in our final scene, Jingles hangs
by the dock where his brother died,

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.400
when he's visited once again by Lavinia.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:53.560
He tells her he thinks about Bobby every
day and reiterates his desire to kill Ricky.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.820
If Jingles is gonna stand a chance
against Ricky, he'll need to kill himself.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:01.980
Now, I felt the show could have done a
better job explaining how this all works,

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.720
but it appears since Jingles
owes a debt to Ricky and Satan,

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.560
if he were killed by them,
he would be gone for good.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:13.860
But if he kills himself, he'll be resurrected at
Camp Rewood and become one of the ghosts.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.920
Jingles feels that if he's going to stand the best
chance of defeating Ricky and protecting his son,

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:24.520
he needs to kill himself, resurrecting in
front of his corpse, ready to take on Ramirez.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.920
That's it for this episode
of "American Horror Story".

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.900
Make sure to like, subscribe, and leave your
thoughts and theories in the comments below.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.920
You can also follow me
on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.640
Until next time remember,

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.340
Daddy loves you very much.

